// Forced piecewise leaves an input it cannot serve after a global solve's minimum budget, priced as Auto's route
// prices it, where the selector would not choose piecewise (PiecewiseRootConfig::caller_method, since 21
// October 2026). The fuzzer's exact case 12759219678555578615 (a cluster
// of 8 roots 2^-42 apart among 13, Gaussian coefficients) at the approximation goal, 16 bits, 100 work units: at a
// 64-bit cap piecewise's precision budget passes the cap and hands the solve to secular, which answers; at twice the
// cap piecewise kept its own rounds until the work budget ended them with one region of all 13 roots, because its
// exit priced the budget at its own work per model-construction unit, some hundred times more. Checked: at both caps
// the goal is met, and at the doubled one by the regime exit's hand-off, inside the work budget.
